This strategy connects directly producers with customers without any intermediaries. It promotes a drastic systemic change by creating alternative conditions to modify habits and behaviours on a local scale. Here, the customers are free to choose where and what they want to buy without having to rely on controlled or imposed logistics. The strategy is characterized by high-quality standards where members collaborate together for everyday logistics activities and more (e.g. members deliver food, work, or manage places and employes). Activities can be carried out physically or through virtual social networks (platform).  The main values in this strategy are collaboration, efficiency and relations between direct producers and customers.